[2] what a flat-ground fit reports when the data came off a slope
==============================================================================
    (this is what every mask-space method implicitly does)
    M   : wind direction reported   70.3 deg (truth 45.0) -> error 25.26 deg     chi2/N = 1.0078
    M+P : wind direction reported   65.9 deg (truth 45.0) -> error 20.93 deg     chi2/N = 2.2216

    the mask-only answer sits within 0.0 deg of the combined
    wind+slope direction (70.2 deg): the mask reported the
    vector sum and called it the wind, exactly as the algebra says it must.

