[2b] the right procedure: let the slope factor float too
==============================================================================
    M   : wind   50.5 deg (err  5.54, restart spread 20.08 deg)   phi_s 0.844 (truth 1.0, err 15.6%)   chi2/N 1.0078
    M+P : wind   45.0 deg (err  0.04, restart spread  0.00 deg)   phi_s 1.003 (truth 1.0, err  0.3%)   chi2/N 1.0072

    Letting the slope float removes the bias, but for masks it only converts
    a confident wrong answer into an unconstrained one: the restart spread is
    20.1 deg against 0.00 deg with the plume.

